.docname {Graphical interface}
.include {docs}

```sh
cargo run --bin gui
```

The Bevy front end shows the same simulation as the CLI, but lets you watch it,
steer it, and edit the board while it runs. It starts from fixed seed `42`.

## Toolbar

A persistent toolbar sits above everything else:

| Control | Behavior |
|---------|----------|
| Play / Pause | Starts and stops automatic turn advancement |
| Step | Pauses, then advances exactly one turn |
| Reset | Pauses and restores the last saved setup, or the board loaded at launch |
| Speed | Chooses the automatic playback rate from a dropdown |
| Fit board | Frames the whole board in the viewport |

Reset reuses the current seed and probabilities. The toolbar's status line
reports the outcome of the most recent save or seed change for a few seconds.

The **Speed** dropdown offers 0.25, 0.5, 1, 2, 5, 10, and 20 turns/s, plus the
launch default of about 2.22 turns/s. A bullet marks the current preset.
Selecting a speed keeps playback running or paused as it was.
.keybinding {[} / .keybinding {]} still halve or double the rate within
0.25–20 turns/s; the dropdown shows the resulting rate even between presets.

Focus the dropdown and press .keybinding {Down} to open it. Use
.keybinding {Up} / .keybinding {Down} or .keybinding {Home} / .keybinding {End}
to navigate, then .keybinding {Enter} or .keybinding {Space} to select.
.keybinding {Escape} dismisses the menu and returns focus to its button.

## Sidebar tabs

The properties sidebar has three tabs: **Overview**, **Parameters**, and **Edit**.
.keybinding {Tab} enters the tab strip. .keybinding {Left} and .keybinding {Right}
switch pages; .keybinding {Home} and .keybinding {End} select the first and last
page. .keybinding {Tab} leaves the strip for the page controls. An underline marks
the selected page, and a focus outline shows keyboard focus.

Aphid, ladybug, and food totals stay visible in the left sidebar in every tab,
alongside how each changed in the last turn.

### Overview

Keeps recent births and deaths, the event list, and the food layer controls in
view. **Run setup** and **Controls & shortcuts** expand when needed.

**Events** lists turns newest first. Each row shows changed parameters with their
before/after percentages and any species extinctions. Rule changes apply after
the named turn; extinctions occur on it. Only events in the chart's latest 240
turns remain in the list.

Select a row to pin the chart's crosshair and population readout to that turn.
Selecting also opens a collapsed chart. Playback continues; this inspects a
recorded turn without rewinding the simulation. **Clear pin** returns to hover
inspection. A pin clears when its event expires or is reverted, and on Reset,
a board edit, or Undo. Undo restores the old events without restoring the pin.
An event at turn zero can be inspected before the first simulation step.

The list scrolls independently of the surrounding panel. .keybinding {Tab}
focuses it; .keybinding {Up} / .keybinding {Down} move through rows,
.keybinding {Home} / .keybinding {End} move to the first/last row, and
.keybinding {Enter} or .keybinding {Space} pins the active row.

**Run setup** shows the seed the run started from plus a field holding a draft
of it. The field takes digits only, up to the 20 digits of `u64::MAX`.
**Restart with this seed**, or .keybinding {Enter} while the field has focus,
applies what is typed and restarts the run from it. A seed that cannot be read
is reported and leaves the run untouched. While the field has focus it keeps
the keyboard, so the playback shortcuts below do not fire as you type.

**Save setup** (.keybinding {S}), in the same section, writes the current
creature positions and probabilities to the same configuration file the CLI
uses, creating parent directories as needed. If that file does not parse, it
is first moved to `simulation.toml.bak`, and the status line says so. Food
values, creature life values, and the current turn are not saved. What is saved
becomes what Reset restores.

If the configuration file is invalid at launch, the GUI opens on the built-in
defaults and the status line reports it until the next message replaces it.

> Note: Reloading a setup from disk without restarting is not implemented.
> Reset restores the last setup saved in this session, or the board loaded at
> launch.

### Parameters

Parameters are grouped by Aphids, Ladybugs, and Environment. Each one has an
editable percentage and a short explanation. The ladybug prey life
gain is not a probability and has no control here. Set it in the
[config file](configuration.qd); Save setup keeps whatever value was loaded.

- .keybinding {Enter} or leaving the field applies a value from 0 to 100.
- Invalid input restores the previous value and reports an error.
- Drag a percentage horizontally to adjust it with one decimal place, or use
  its − / + buttons for 0.1 percentage-point steps.
- Typed values retain finer precision; focusing a field does not round it.
- A bullet marks values changed from the saved setup.
- Each group has **Restore defaults** for the built-in values.
- A successful Save setup updates the saved-value baseline.

The settings area scrolls with the wheel or its scrollbar, while the tabs and
toolbar stay visible.

### Edit

Illustrated **Aphid** (.keybinding {A}) and **Ladybug** (.keybinding {L}) tools
place creatures; **Erase** (.keybinding {X}) clears them.

Choosing a tool pauses the simulation and shows a placement preview on the
board. Left click places a creature, right click removes one of the selected
species, and Erase removes all creatures in the cell while leaving its food.
Dragging still pans the board. **Done** leaves editing paused; Play resumes it.

Each edit restarts the turn count and chart. **Undo edit** (.keybinding {Z})
restores the previous board, creature life, food, random-number state, and
history, keeping the run paused and the current parameter settings. Up to 20
edits can be undone; advancing a turn or resetting clears that undo history.

## Board views

**Population** view uses neutral cells to emphasize creatures. **Food** view
shades cells by food supply and offers optional, subdued bars and speckles.
Creatures get a dark backing for contrast in both views. .keybinding {F}
switches to Food view and toggles its details.

When cells are smaller than 28 logical pixels, illustrated creatures collapse
into one marker per occupied cell and species: green circles for aphids and red
diamonds for ladybugs. Mixed cells keep both markers. Zooming in restores the
detailed sprites and the count badges for crowded cells.

Hovering a cell opens the cell inspector as a popup beside the pointer, so
inspecting a cell never moves the controls.

Scroll over the board to zoom, drag with the left or middle mouse button to
pan, and use **Fit board** (.keybinding {Home}) to frame the whole board again.

## Population chart

The chart draws aphids as a solid line and ladybugs as a dashed one, keeping
the latest 240 turns.

- Diamonds mark rule changes after a turn.
- Crosses mark a species going extinct on that turn.
- Hovering reads out population counts and event summaries unless an event is pinned.
- Changes to the same parameter between turns share one event, and reverting
  them removes that change.
- Events expire with the rolling history and are restored along with history by
  edit Undo.

**Hide chart** / **Show chart** gives the board more room, **Height −** and
**Height +** resize it, and the chart's top edge can be dragged. Resizing keeps
at least 180 logical pixels for the board. Until a run has enough history to
plot, the chart displays a prompt; collapsing it keeps collecting history.

## Keyboard shortcuts

| Key | Action |
|-----|--------|
| .keybinding {Space} | Play / pause |
| .keybinding {N} | Step one turn |
| .keybinding {R} | Reset |
| .keybinding {S} | Save setup |
| .keybinding {[} / .keybinding {]} | Slower / faster |
| .keybinding {Home} | Fit board |
| .keybinding {F} | Toggle Food view and its details |
| .keybinding {E} | Open the edit controls |
| .keybinding {A} / .keybinding {L} / .keybinding {X} | Aphid, ladybug, erase tool |
| .keybinding {Z} | Undo edit |

.keybinding {Space} activates the focused widget when one has focus. Click the
board or press .keybinding {Escape} to return to global .keybinding {Space}
playback.

## Appearance

Text is set in Fira Sans, which ships embedded in `bevy_feathers`. The design
notes and trade-offs behind the board renderer are recorded in
.repolink {notes/bevy-board-rendering.md} {blob/main/notes/bevy-board-rendering.md}.
